# Sitting 4c's damaged panels.pak (sim-fidelity.md "Device surprises" 6):
# the device's read-only fsck found the file's cluster chain ending after
# 2 clusters (32 KB) while its directory entry said 5,407,744 B, the rest
# of the chain free, 61 orphaned clusters: a write cut after the size was
# updated and before the chain was completed.  Its header still passed,
# so the builder wrote slots in place past the cut and every PP panel
# build failed (ok=0), pass after pass.  "fs_chaincut" gives the sim's
# file the same damage (filesystem-sim.c: the size and lseek kept, reads
# and writes past the chain's end refused); the builder must notice at
# load (the last byte does not read) and recover panels.pak.prev or
# start the set over in a new file, never write into the cut one.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui-video scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p19-panels-chaincut.script
# needs: library
# golden: skip
# timeout: 300
# logbetween: c0 end art panels chain cut: tail unreadable
# logbetween: c0 end art panels chain cut: (prev recovered|set rebuilt)
# logbetween: c0 end fs_chaincut /.rockbox/artcache/panels.pak whole
# logbetween: c0 end expect_panels_valid ok
# nolog: fs_chaincut /.rockbox/artcache/panels.pak cut
# nolog: expect_panels_valid failed
# nolog: art retain panels
wait 1000
wait_db 30000
art_wait 120000
expect_panels_valid
ab_mark c0
fs_chaincut /.rockbox/artcache/panels.pak 32768
art_request         # the next pass loads the set
wait 1000
art_wait 120000
fs_chaincut /.rockbox/artcache/panels.pak check
expect_panels_valid
shot end            # one shot so shots.sh counts the run (golden: skip)
quit
